  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 816b4954867bc40e39ad7c562a837967, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: '::'
  logs:
  - "Log 1\n\n09-03-2025, 17:43\n\nProgress is slower than I anticipated. My hands
    are getting worse by the day, and fine motor control is becoming a problem. I
    managed to secure an off-market compound for the panacea project: Nocropro. If
    the reports are accurate, it may help regenerate damaged dopamine pathways. I\u2019ll
    begin trials on the mice tonight."
  - "Log 2\n\n09-10-2025, 03:32\n\nProgress. Real progress. The mice exposed to Nocropro
    show increased neuron density and improved muscle function. The results are better
    than I hoped. If this continues, I may finally have something that works. Maybe
    then Madeleine will see I\u2019m not beyond saving."
  - "Log 3\n\n09-12-2025, 07:30\n\nThe mice are stronger. Faster, too. But they\u2019ve
    become aggressive\u2014violently aggressive. Their behavior is beginning to resemble
    rabid animals. I should stop. I know I should. But I\u2019m too close now. Animal
    trials can only tell me so much. The next step requires a human subject."
  - "Log 4\n\n09-14-2025, 15:00\n\nHuman trials have begun. On myself. The tremors
    are fading. My reflexes are sharper, my body feels\u2026 lighter. Stronger. For
    the first time in months, I feel capable again. There are unusual growths appearing
    on the mice, but those complications may be incidental. What matters is that
    this is working. It has to be working."
  - "Log 5\n\n10-01-2025, 17:00\n\nMy symptoms came back. Worse than before. I was
    so close. So close. The strength is still there, but it\u2019s changing me. There
    are growths along my back now. Muscle spasms. Bursts of anger I can\u2019t control.
    I should have paid attention to the mice. God... I should have paid attention."
  - 'Log 6


    Undated


    Madeleine... URGHHHH AHHH'
  logTextUI: {fileID: 1251404283}
  logPanel: {fileID: 1769854653}
